---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
const posts = await getCollection("technical");

const sortedPosts = posts.sort(
  (a, b) => b.data.pubDate.valueOf() - a.data.pubDate.valueOf(),
);

import Navbar from "../../components/Navbar/Navbar.astro";
import DocHeader from "../../components/DocHeader/DocHeader.astro";
import DocFooter from "../../components/DocFooter/DocFooter.astro";
---

<style>
  article {
    justify-content: space-between;
    border: 1px solid black;
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 1rem;

    h2 {
      margin-top: 0;
    }

    * {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
    }
    a {
      margin-top: 10px;
    }
  }
</style>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <DocHeader />
    <title>Adam Hardie - Technical Posts</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <Navbar />
    <h1>Tech posts</h1>
    <p>
      The intention behind my technical posts is to get some real, human content
      out into the world. In this weird age of AI, we're seeing vast amounts of
      AI generated content flooding feeds, from linkedin and medium, to stack
      overflow and beyond.
    </p>
    <p>
      My technical skill set, while ever growing, is definitely not perfect and
      I'm open to new ideas and approaches. I do not think anything here should
      be taken as gospel, nor do I think I have particularly unique takes, but
      what I do have is a desire to become a much better engineer.
    </p>
    <p>
      This will be real-world discussions around things I find interesting and
      challenges I've faced in work or personal projects.
    </p>
    <section>
      {
        sortedPosts.map((post) => (
          <article>
            <h2>{post.data.title}</h2>
            <p>{post.data.description}</p>
            <time datetime={post.data.pubDate.toISOString()}>
              {post.data.pubDate.toDateString()}
            </time>
            <a href={`/technical/${post.id}/`}>Read more</a>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </section>
    <DocFooter />
  </body>
</html>
